# Line-ending policy (OPS-09).
#
# `text=auto` means: store text files with LF in the repository, check them out
# platform-native. A file normalizes the next time anyone stages it, so the
# CRLF/LF drift this repo accumulated (it started on Windows and moved to
# macOS) cannot grow.
#
# The one-shot `git add --renormalize .` over the ~880 files that were already
# committed as CRLF IS DONE: 2026-09-08, commit 5638a977, 879 files. This
# header used to say it had NOT been done, which stayed wrong for a day and
# then for longer -- see docs/ops/CRLF_NORMALIZATION.md, which now records both
# halves. `.git-blame-ignore-revs` carries that SHA so blame still works.
#
# backend/tests/unit/test_line_endings_stay_lf.py fails the build if a CRLF
# blob is ever committed again.

* text=auto

# Explicitly text, so a file whose first bytes look binary is not misdetected.
*.py     text
*.js     text
*.jsx    text
*.ts     text
*.tsx    text
*.json   text
*.md     text
*.sql    text
*.yml    text
*.yaml   text
*.html   text
*.css    text
*.mjs    text
*.cjs    text

# Shell scripts are LF even on Windows -- a CRLF shebang line does not execute.
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Binary -- never touch these.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.svg    text
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks    binary
*.hbc    binary
